/**
 * KINDRED DOMINANCE (play-weighted #701; Kindred Judgment prints the same text) and ELDRITCH EVOLUTION (#756).
 *
 * KINDRED DOMINANCE — "Choose a creature type. Destroy all creatures that aren't of the chosen type."
 *   One atom, destroy-not-chosen-type (templateMatchers.matchDestroyNotChosenType — the second sentence reads the first one's
 *   choice, so the two collapse together). At resolution (removal.js):
 *  - THE CHOICE (CR 608.2d — made as the spell resolves; CR 205.3e — one existing creature type, the CR 205.3m list):
 *    choicePolicy.autoPickCreatureTypeToSpare — the type with the most of the caster's creatures net of the other players',
 *    then the most of the caster's own, then the first in sorted order; one type nobody has stands for "spare nothing".
 *  - THE SET: every permanent that is a creature right now and is not of the chosen type. Types are current ones
 *    (layers.permanentCreatureTypes, CR 613.1d): an added type counts, a replaced type does not, a double-faced creature has its
 *    front face's (CR 712.8d), a copy has the copied ones (CR 707.2). Every creature type — Changeling (CR 702.73a), an
 *    all-creature-types effect — is of the chosen type whatever was chosen.
 *  - THE DESTROY: the shared applyDestroyEffect, one event — indestructible (CR 702.12b), regeneration (CR 701.8c) and umbra
 *    armor (CR 702.89a) apply as to any destroy.
 *
 * ELDRITCH EVOLUTION — "As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature. / Search your library for a creature
 *   card with mana value X or less, where X is 2 plus the sacrificed creature's mana value. Put that card onto the battlefield,
 *   then shuffle. Exile Eldritch Evolution."
 *   The cost is the existing single-victim sacrifice lane (legalChoices offers one cast per victim, actionDispatcher pays it).
 *   One tutor atom (templateMatchers.matchTutorMvCapFromSacrificed) capped at 2 + the sacrificed creature's last-known mana
 *   value (CR 608.2h), which the dispatcher now freezes on the spell itself as the cost is paid; the trailing sentence is the
 *   parser's selfExile stamp. The mana value is the object's as it was sacrificed (layers.permanentManaValue): a token that is
 *   not a copy has 0 (CR 202.1b, 202.3a), a copy has the copied value (CR 707.2), an {X} in a cost is 0 (CR 107.3g, 202.3e).
 *   The found card enters through zones.enterCardFromZone, so its entry replacements apply.
 *
 * Real oracle fixtures (bundled Scryfall data, generated by cardIndex.publicCard — never typed by hand). Board states (a regen
 * shield, an attachment, a bestowed Aura, a chosen type stamped as the entry would) are built directly where a test says so;
 * the SYNTHETIC tests are labelled.
 */
